-- title:
--   Dusart finite-range certificate data, block 21
-- statement:
--   Certificate data block 21 of 24 for the finite-range check of Dusart's bound for $\sum_{p\le x}1/p$ on $[10372,3594641]$: a list of wheel blocks, each a list of factor codes for consecutive integers coprime to $210$ (code $0$ for a prime, otherwise its smallest prime factor) together with an optional mesh-cell check (the exponents used for the logarithm range reductions).
--
--   The data are produced by a program and are checked, not trusted: the accompanying theorem `DusartCert.run_21` states the result of running the kernel checker `DusartCert.run` on this block.
-- source:
--   P. Dusart, Estimates of some functions over primes without R.H., arXiv:1002.0442 (2010), Theorem 6.10 (upper bound for x ≥ 10372) and Theorem 5.2 (k = 2, η = 0.2, x ≥ 3 594 641); the proof of Theorem 6.10 closes the range below 3 594 641 by a computer check.

